      "created_at": "2023-09-21T20:18:19.062Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Welcome to the community, Albavar! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\"></p>\n<p>Unfortunately, Adobe doesn’t allow images in dropdowns for Acrobat files. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/cry.png?v=12\" title=\":cry:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":cry:\"> It’s possible to do it with some JavaScripting and other customizations, but no one has had the combination of skills and time to do that, to date.</p>\n<p>I usually insert the icon I want manually, which isn’t as convenient but it looks pretty good. The icons are available in a few places, but I have them up here: <a href=\"http://www.luzetski.net/SCRPG/SCRPG_icons.zip\">http://www.luzetski.net/SCRPG/SCRPG_icons.zip</a>. (Link fixed for now. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/frowning.png?v=12\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\"> )</p>",
